    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "643d3c8e_b2a998f6",
        "filename": "chip/mec1701/espi.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 772,
      "author": {
        "id": 1174219
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-08T17:19:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Infinite while loops are bad! Implemented new code polling for master reading changed vwire a finite number of times with delay between polls. Currently 50 loops with 10 us delay. Worst case in production is 20MHz eSPI clock, one lane, and max payload size of 64 bytes. In development host chipset can be strapped to 8MHz eSPI clock.",
      "revId": "061ab8555f68be49606aa74c701a73d42823193a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "172bf8c4_3bd78d52",
        "filename": "chip/mec1701/espi.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1478,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-24T16:14:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that there is an implicit 1-second timeout when the EC watchdog will kick in and reboot the entire system.\n\nIt might be better to have a timeout shorter than that which forces the AP back to G3.\n\nAlternately, we might need to split G3S5 into two states, with the transition between them being epsi_chan_ready().  Or can you just block the transition from G3S5 to S5 until espi_chan_ready() without spin-waiting?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1467,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1478,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "061ab8555f68be49606aa74c701a73d42823193a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "158af787_b7c85ca1",
        "filename": "chip/mec1701/espi.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1478,
      "author": {
        "id": 1174219
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-08T17:24:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have removed espi_wait_ready, espi_chan_ready and HOOK_CHIPSET_PRE_INT because the power state machine waits up to 10 seconds for SLP_S4# (a virtual wire) to de-assert. This should be more than enough time for eSPI master to bring up the link and send the new SLP_Sx virtual wire states.  New code is working on our KBL + MEC1701 EVB fly wire setup.",
      "parentUuid": "172bf8c4_3bd78d52",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1467,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1478,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "061ab8555f68be49606aa74c701a73d42823193a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
